# edgelab second instance — Pepperstone cTrader DEMO, EUR+BTC (~$5k). Copy to .env, then chmod 600 .env.
#
# Recommended order (no footgun now): copy this file to .env, fill the two Telegram lines + EDGELAB_LABEL,
# then run examples/ctrader_get_token.py. It MERGES into .env (updates the CTRADER_* token lines and
# leaves everything else — Telegram, label, token store — intact). It no longer overwrites the whole file.
#
# --- Pepperstone cTrader Open API app -------------------------------------------------------------
# Use a SEPARATE app from the FP Markets bot (its own Client ID/Secret). Two bots must never share one
# cTrader token: cTrader rotates the refresh token, so a shared token means they revoke each other.
CTRADER_CLIENT_ID=
CTRADER_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# --- Filled by examples/ctrader_get_token.py (or paste by hand) -----------------------------------
# ACCOUNT_ID is the ctidTraderAccountId of the DEMO account (the token script auto-discovers it; it is
# NOT the broker "login" number you see in the Pepperstone portal).
CTRADER_ACCESS_TOKEN=
CTRADER_REFRESH_TOKEN=
CTRADER_ACCOUNT_ID=
#
# Isolated token store for THIS instance, relative to the service WorkingDirectory. Keep it distinct
# from the main bot's so the two never touch the same token file.
CTRADER_TOKEN_STORE=.ctrader_refresh_token
#
# --- Telegram -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reuse the main bot's bot token + chat id, and set EDGELAB_LABEL so you can tell the two bots apart in
# one chat. (Or create a second bot via BotFather and put ITS token here instead, and drop EDGELAB_LABEL.)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
EDGELAB_LABEL=[pepper-eurbtc]
